WEBVTT

00:00:07.374 --> 00:00:09.433
When the Captain told us
to start collecting deuterium,

00:00:09.476 --> 00:00:11.273
Seven suggested a series
of modifications

00:00:11.311 --> 00:00:12.676
to the Bussard collectors.

00:00:12.712 --> 00:00:14.737
Problem is, l didn't realize
the extent of the modifications

00:00:14.781 --> 00:00:16.544
until after we'd begun
the sweep...

00:00:16.583 --> 00:00:18.278
l mean, not that there was
anything wrong with them.

00:00:18.318 --> 00:00:19.979
In fact, efficiency
is up 23 percent.

00:00:20.020 --> 00:00:21.214
In a nutshell, Harry.

00:00:21.254 --> 00:00:23.245
The collectors are almost full,

00:00:23.289 --> 00:00:24.620
but l can't tell
exactly how full

00:00:24.657 --> 00:00:26.386
until l realign my sensors
with Seven's.

00:00:26.426 --> 00:00:29.190
Why didn't you
just say so?

00:00:29.229 --> 00:00:31.254
Next time, work closer
with her from the start.

00:00:32.866 --> 00:00:35.300
Closer. Right.

00:00:35.335 --> 00:00:39.635
So, you're going to realign
your sensors with Seven's.

00:00:39.672 --> 00:00:41.765
Sounds like fun.

00:00:41.808 --> 00:00:43.503
Very funny.

00:00:44.511 --> 00:00:46.741
What was that?

00:00:46.780 --> 00:00:49.806
Are you getting feedback
from Seven's modifications?

00:00:49.849 --> 00:00:51.817
Negative.

00:00:51.851 --> 00:00:53.284
Report.

00:00:53.319 --> 00:00:56.584
L am picking up proton surges
just outside the ship.

00:00:56.623 --> 00:00:58.386
The first was
off the port beam,

00:00:58.425 --> 00:01:00.325
and the second two were
off the starboard bow.

00:01:00.360 --> 00:01:01.588
On screen.

00:01:01.628 --> 00:01:04.324
There's nothing out there.

00:01:04.364 --> 00:01:06.889
Whatever it is,
it's getting closer.

00:01:06.933 --> 00:01:09.265
Red Alert.
Janeway to Astrometrics.

00:01:09.302 --> 00:01:10.428
Yes, Captain.

00:01:10.470 --> 00:01:13.268
Use the astrometric sensors
to scan for the disturbance.

00:01:15.275 --> 00:01:17.539
L'm detecting
close-range weapons fire.

00:01:17.577 --> 00:01:19.306
Source?

00:01:19.345 --> 00:01:24.112
Proton surges suggest two
cloaked ships engaged in battle.

00:01:24.150 --> 00:01:25.082
With us caught in the middle.

00:01:25.118 --> 00:01:26.449
Evasive maneuvers.

00:01:26.486 --> 00:01:27.453
Aye, sir.

00:01:27.487 --> 00:01:28.681
There's a massive
power surge...

00:01:28.721 --> 00:01:30.848
like one of the
ships is exploding.

00:01:34.461 --> 00:01:35.894
Captain,

00:01:35.929 --> 00:01:37.556
there is one life sign aboard

00:01:37.597 --> 00:01:38.586
that vessel.

00:01:41.668 --> 00:01:43.533
It is no longer on our sensors.

00:01:43.570 --> 00:01:45.538
We're being hailed...
audio only.

00:01:45.572 --> 00:01:46.732
Let's hear it.

00:01:46.773 --> 00:01:49.901
Chakotay, please,
l need your help.

00:03:49.361 --> 00:03:51.989
Chakotay, are you reading me?

00:03:52.030 --> 00:03:53.725
Please answer.

00:03:53.765 --> 00:03:55.926
This is Commander Chakotay.

00:03:55.968 --> 00:03:57.128
Who are you?

00:03:57.169 --> 00:03:59.160
Please, anyone on Voyager,

00:03:59.204 --> 00:04:01.229
if you can hear me, l need help.

00:04:03.508 --> 00:04:05.237
There has been
an explosion on the vessel.

00:04:05.277 --> 00:04:06.904
The hull is
destabilizing.

00:04:06.945 --> 00:04:07.809
Life support
is off-line.

00:04:07.846 --> 00:04:09.370
Beam her directly to Sick Bay.

00:04:09.414 --> 00:04:11.041
Targeting her
coordinates.

00:04:13.051 --> 00:04:14.882
L've lost her.
Trying again.

00:04:16.722 --> 00:04:18.053
L don't understand.

00:04:18.090 --> 00:04:19.489
L get a clear lock;
then it drops out.

00:04:19.524 --> 00:04:21.583
If we can get
an away team over there,

00:04:21.626 --> 00:04:23.526
we could stabilize her ship
and tractor it in.

00:04:23.562 --> 00:04:24.551
Do it.

00:04:24.596 --> 00:04:27.690
Tom, Tuvok, let's find out
what's going on.

00:04:44.616 --> 00:04:47.551
Environmental systems
are not functioning.

00:04:47.586 --> 00:04:50.248
Oxygen levels are
dangerously low.

00:04:50.288 --> 00:04:51.983
Tom...

00:04:52.090 --> 00:04:53.955
try to get
life support on line.

00:04:53.992 --> 00:04:55.550
No life signs.

00:04:55.594 --> 00:04:57.892
See if you can
stabilize the hull.

00:04:59.097 --> 00:05:00.724
L'll look for the pilot.

00:05:03.201 --> 00:05:04.361
Hello?

00:05:07.606 --> 00:05:09.335
Can you hear me?

00:05:09.374 --> 00:05:12.036
Chakotay, is it you?

00:05:16.281 --> 00:05:17.680
Yes.

00:05:17.716 --> 00:05:20.708
L'm going to get
this bulkhead off you.

00:05:20.752 --> 00:05:22.652
But the beam will fall.

00:05:28.427 --> 00:05:30.418
L'm going to pry the bulkhead
off you.

00:05:34.199 --> 00:05:37.657
When l say "now," get ready
to roll out of there

00:05:37.702 --> 00:05:39.192
like your life depended on it.

00:05:39.237 --> 00:05:40.204
All right.

00:05:40.238 --> 00:05:41.227
Ready?

00:05:41.273 --> 00:05:42.900
Yes.

00:05:42.941 --> 00:05:44.636
Now!

00:05:53.218 --> 00:05:55.345
L knew you'd come.

00:05:55.387 --> 00:05:57.184
Do l know you?

00:06:00.358 --> 00:06:01.882
Chakotay to Voyager.

00:06:01.927 --> 00:06:03.827
Two to beam directly
to Sick Bay.

00:06:22.180 --> 00:06:23.169
How is she?

00:06:23.215 --> 00:06:24.739
L'm not certain.

00:06:24.783 --> 00:06:26.182
When l scan her,
the readings

00:06:26.218 --> 00:06:28.049
won't stay
in the database.

00:06:28.086 --> 00:06:30.782
Luckily, l'm a master
of visual diagnosis.

00:06:30.822 --> 00:06:31.948
She has a minor
concussion

00:06:31.990 --> 00:06:33.457
and a compound
tibular fracture...

00:06:33.492 --> 00:06:34.789
nothing
life-threatening.

00:06:34.826 --> 00:06:36.384
L can repair
the damage.

00:06:36.428 --> 00:06:37.952
Did you find out
how she knows you?

00:06:38.029 --> 00:06:39.360
Not yet.

00:06:41.166 --> 00:06:42.997
No.

00:06:44.002 --> 00:06:45.333
L can't.

00:06:47.572 --> 00:06:49.506
She's coming around.

00:06:55.580 --> 00:06:56.979
Don't be frightened.

00:06:57.015 --> 00:06:58.209
You're quite safe here.

00:07:05.390 --> 00:07:10.692
Captain... please...
l need asylum.

00:07:10.729 --> 00:07:12.094
You must let me stay
on your ship

00:07:12.130 --> 00:07:13.222
and we've got to get away

00:07:13.265 --> 00:07:14.232
from here.

00:07:14.266 --> 00:07:15.255
They'll be coming
after me.

00:07:15.300 --> 00:07:16.289
Slow down a minute.

00:07:16.334 --> 00:07:18.564
L have a few questions first.

00:07:18.603 --> 00:07:20.696
Who are you?

00:07:20.739 --> 00:07:23.264
And how do you know
my First Officer?

00:07:23.308 --> 00:07:25.606
Lt's a complicated story.

00:07:27.512 --> 00:07:29.412
L'm not...

00:07:29.447 --> 00:07:31.642
l'm not sure...

00:07:31.683 --> 00:07:34.151
quite how to begin.

00:07:34.186 --> 00:07:37.883
But if you don't give me asylum,
they're going to track me down

00:07:37.923 --> 00:07:39.891
and they're going
to take me back.

00:07:39.925 --> 00:07:42.587
And l don't want to go.

00:07:42.627 --> 00:07:46.063
We won't turn you over to anyone
without knowing the whole story.

00:07:48.633 --> 00:07:49.930
Thank you.

00:07:49.968 --> 00:07:52.493
Chakotay.

00:07:52.537 --> 00:07:54.698
L want you to
stay with her.

00:07:54.739 --> 00:07:56.570
She seems to trust you.

00:07:56.608 --> 00:07:57.973
Maybe you'll be
able to find out

00:07:58.009 --> 00:07:58.976
what this
is all about.

00:07:59.010 --> 00:08:01.069
L hope so.

00:08:01.112 --> 00:08:02.511
Keep me informed.

00:08:08.687 --> 00:08:09.915
Once l've repaired
the fracture,

00:08:10.021 --> 00:08:11.488
she'll need
some bed rest.

00:08:12.490 --> 00:08:14.424
Will you stay with me?

00:08:14.459 --> 00:08:16.051
Of course.

00:08:17.195 --> 00:08:18.856
Then l'll be fine.

00:08:19.965 --> 00:08:20.932
There.

00:08:20.966 --> 00:08:22.490
That should do it.

00:08:22.534 --> 00:08:25.196
L'd ask you to monitor
her vital signs,

00:08:25.237 --> 00:08:26.602
but since they
aren't registering,

00:08:26.638 --> 00:08:27.832
l suppose there's no point.

00:08:31.009 --> 00:08:33.239
Well... l have
several days' worth

00:08:33.278 --> 00:08:34.939
of inoculation records
to catalog.

00:08:34.980 --> 00:08:36.277
L suppose l'll get to it.

00:08:40.552 --> 00:08:42.019
Is he gone?

00:08:43.989 --> 00:08:45.149
Yes.

00:08:45.190 --> 00:08:47.852
Then we're alone.

00:08:47.892 --> 00:08:49.689
In a manner of speaking.

00:08:51.763 --> 00:08:53.628
Can you start clearing
up a few things now?

00:08:53.665 --> 00:08:55.633
L'll try.

00:08:57.435 --> 00:08:59.335
It's complicated.

00:09:01.673 --> 00:09:05.006
You see... we've met before.

00:09:05.043 --> 00:09:08.137
If that were true,
l'm sure l'd remember.

00:09:08.179 --> 00:09:09.908
No, you wouldn't.

00:09:10.015 --> 00:09:11.778
You couldn't.

00:09:14.686 --> 00:09:17.746
You see,
the memories of my people

00:09:17.789 --> 00:09:20.917
can't be held in the minds
of other races.

00:09:20.992 --> 00:09:23.654
When we encounter others,

00:09:23.695 --> 00:09:25.595
which we do...

00:09:25.630 --> 00:09:27.530
infrequently,

00:09:27.565 --> 00:09:30.659
they remember us
for a few hours...

00:09:30.702 --> 00:09:33.694
but then the memories fade away.

00:09:33.738 --> 00:09:38.038
We're completely forgotten
by the next day.

00:09:38.076 --> 00:09:41.273
Is this done through technology?
Telepathy?

00:09:41.313 --> 00:09:43.838
Lt's a factor of our biology.

00:09:43.882 --> 00:09:47.409
You see, our bodies produce
a sort of pheromone,

00:09:47.452 --> 00:09:51.252
which blocks the long-term
memory engrams of others.

00:09:51.289 --> 00:09:53.814
Is that why the tricorder
can't scan you?

00:09:53.858 --> 00:09:55.883
Why we couldn't get
a transporter lock?

00:09:55.927 --> 00:09:59.090
We're impervious
to those sort of devices.

00:09:59.130 --> 00:10:01.257
Your ships are cloaked as well.

00:10:01.299 --> 00:10:03.597
When you live
a covert existence,

00:10:03.635 --> 00:10:07.696
you develop technology
to enhance it.

00:10:10.008 --> 00:10:11.737
But you say we've met before.

00:10:11.776 --> 00:10:13.971
About a month ago.

00:10:14.079 --> 00:10:17.014
L spent several weeks here.

00:10:19.551 --> 00:10:20.950
Several weeks?

00:10:20.985 --> 00:10:23.180
You and l worked
closely together.

00:10:23.221 --> 00:10:26.088
You helped me
a great deal.

00:10:26.124 --> 00:10:27.887
Then l left...

00:10:29.461 --> 00:10:32.624
knowing that you would forget
everything about me.

00:10:34.165 --> 00:10:35.689
Then why did you come back?

00:10:35.734 --> 00:10:37.599
Why the battle?
Why ask us for asylum?

00:10:37.635 --> 00:10:38.602
L know you want

00:10:38.636 --> 00:10:40.729
everything in a nutshell.

00:10:40.772 --> 00:10:43.206
That's the way you work.

00:10:43.241 --> 00:10:45.436
But l have to tell you
the whole story

00:10:45.477 --> 00:10:47.274
before it will
make sense.

00:10:47.312 --> 00:10:49.746
Fine. L'm listening.

00:10:51.149 --> 00:10:52.946
L came back...

00:10:54.819 --> 00:10:57.413
because l fell in love with you.

00:11:08.533 --> 00:11:10.160
She comes from Ramura.

00:11:10.201 --> 00:11:11.964
It's a closed society

00:11:12.070 --> 00:11:14.231
that won't tolerate
anybody trying to leave.

00:11:14.272 --> 00:11:17.571
Apparently, she was disenchanted
with that and wanted out.

00:11:17.609 --> 00:11:19.406
They're trying
to bring her back.

00:11:19.444 --> 00:11:21.435
That's why she's asking
for asylum.

00:11:21.479 --> 00:11:23.413
But you say
that she claims

00:11:23.448 --> 00:11:25.313
she was on Voyager
before this.

00:11:25.350 --> 00:11:26.612
About a month ago.

00:11:26.651 --> 00:11:28.881
She says she's a "tracer"...

00:11:28.920 --> 00:11:31.081
a kind of bounty hunter
who tracks down people

00:11:31.122 --> 00:11:32.555
who try to leave their world.

00:11:32.590 --> 00:11:35.354
She found a runaway
hiding on Voyager.

00:11:35.393 --> 00:11:38.362
She was here,
but nobody remembers it?

00:11:38.396 --> 00:11:40.421
That's what she says,
but l think we have to find

00:11:40.465 --> 00:11:41.864
a way to verify
her story.

00:11:41.900 --> 00:11:43.527
L was looking
at her ship.

00:11:43.568 --> 00:11:46.196
It uses a sophisticated
polarization technique

00:11:46.237 --> 00:11:49.331
that causes our sensor scans
to pass right through it.

00:11:49.374 --> 00:11:51.137
She could have
been shadowing us

00:11:51.176 --> 00:11:52.404
for quite
a while.

00:11:52.444 --> 00:11:53.604
And learned enough about us

00:11:53.645 --> 00:11:55.272
to convince us
she's been here before.

00:11:55.313 --> 00:11:56.575
But why?

00:11:56.614 --> 00:11:57.979
Why go to that trouble?

00:11:58.016 --> 00:12:01.679
What about the battle
with that other cloaked ship?

00:12:01.719 --> 00:12:03.812
She put herself in danger

00:12:03.855 --> 00:12:05.720
when it would have
been a lot easier

00:12:05.757 --> 00:12:07.122
simply to ask for asylum.

00:12:07.158 --> 00:12:08.523
L agree...

00:12:08.560 --> 00:12:09.959
but l think
we have to make sure

00:12:10.061 --> 00:12:11.722
she doesn't have
some hidden agenda.

00:12:11.763 --> 00:12:14.596
If she was here, there should
be some evidence of it.

00:12:14.632 --> 00:12:17.692
She said a computer
virus was planted

00:12:17.735 --> 00:12:19.965
to wipe all references
to her being here,

00:12:20.004 --> 00:12:22.438
but l have to believe
we can at least turn up

00:12:22.474 --> 00:12:23.372
some evidence of tampering.

00:12:23.408 --> 00:12:25.376
Harry, Tuvok.
Tom,

00:12:25.410 --> 00:12:27.139
do the same
with her ship.

00:12:27.178 --> 00:12:29.976
See if the navigational logs
support what she's saying.

00:12:30.081 --> 00:12:31.514
Gentlemen.

00:12:34.352 --> 00:12:36.411
L agree we should
take precautions,

00:12:36.454 --> 00:12:39.218
but you seem very
suspicious of her.

00:12:39.257 --> 00:12:40.986
L want to make sure
we're not being manipulated.

00:12:41.059 --> 00:12:42.993
L agree.

00:12:43.061 --> 00:12:44.790
If we grant her asylum,

00:12:44.829 --> 00:12:47.127
we'll be in the position
of having to protect her.

00:12:47.165 --> 00:12:48.462
If we're going to commit
to that,

00:12:48.500 --> 00:12:50.764
we should certainly find out
if she's telling the truth.

00:12:50.802 --> 00:12:53.270
L'd appreciate your thoughts
on that.

00:12:53.304 --> 00:12:54.896
Aye, Captain.

00:12:58.743 --> 00:13:00.108
L have successfully
downloaded

00:13:00.144 --> 00:13:02.237
the navigational logs
from your vessel.

00:13:02.280 --> 00:13:04.077
Good. Now, compare them
with your own logs

00:13:04.115 --> 00:13:05.241
over the last two months.

00:13:05.283 --> 00:13:08.275
Display Voyager's route
toward the Alpha Quadrant.

00:13:09.821 --> 00:13:11.379
Now overlay my route.

00:13:12.957 --> 00:13:14.948
There, you see?

00:13:14.993 --> 00:13:17.052
Our ships traveled together
for at least two weeks.

00:13:17.095 --> 00:13:20.428
You could have falsified
your navigational logs.

00:13:20.465 --> 00:13:22.558
There is no proof that you
ever came aboard Voyager.

00:13:22.600 --> 00:13:25.160
That's what l always liked
about you two...

00:13:25.203 --> 00:13:28.969
such unyielding logic,
such refreshing skepticism.

00:13:29.073 --> 00:13:30.540
Run a diagnostic on my logs.

00:13:30.575 --> 00:13:32.600
You'll find
they haven't been altered.

00:13:33.811 --> 00:13:35.403
How's it going?

00:13:35.446 --> 00:13:37.311
Her story seems
to be legitimate,

00:13:37.348 --> 00:13:39.248
but there are
further steps to take.

00:13:39.284 --> 00:13:40.308
Then take them.

00:13:40.351 --> 00:13:42.376
L thought you might like
to get something to eat...

00:13:42.420 --> 00:13:44.388
unless your memories
of our Mess Hall aren't good.

00:13:44.422 --> 00:13:45.446
As a matter of fact,

00:13:45.490 --> 00:13:47.253
l was quite fond
of Neelix's food.

00:13:47.292 --> 00:13:49.021
Now, that's something
that's hard to believe.

00:13:53.831 --> 00:13:55.992
Commander Chakotay's
face became flushed

00:13:56.100 --> 00:13:57.567
as he spoke with her.

00:13:57.602 --> 00:13:59.194
What does that signify?

00:13:59.237 --> 00:14:01.501
L'd rather not engage
in speculation.

00:14:01.539 --> 00:14:03.564
It is a dangerous pastime.

00:14:09.780 --> 00:14:12.044
L think our guest
will enjoy this, Commander...

00:14:12.082 --> 00:14:15.245
uh, fried soy meal,
buttered carrots

00:14:15.285 --> 00:14:17.549
and a delightful almond pudding.

00:14:17.588 --> 00:14:18.816
Sounds wonderful.

00:14:18.856 --> 00:14:20.619
Very nice.
Thanks, Neelix.

00:14:22.059 --> 00:14:23.924
You were very diplomatic.

00:14:23.961 --> 00:14:25.121
Why do you say that?

00:14:25.162 --> 00:14:27.960
You hate carrots;
fried food upsets your stomach;

00:14:28.032 --> 00:14:31.798
and you refuse to eat pudding
because you think it's slimy.

00:14:31.835 --> 00:14:34.030
Right?

00:14:35.939 --> 00:14:36.963
L'm curious.

00:14:37.041 --> 00:14:39.202
When you were here before,
you said we worked together,

00:14:39.243 --> 00:14:41.370
but you also said you were
here to retrieve a runaway.

00:14:41.412 --> 00:14:43.107
How was l involved?

00:14:43.147 --> 00:14:44.546
Aren't you more curious

00:14:44.581 --> 00:14:46.640
to hear about
how we fell in love?

00:14:46.684 --> 00:14:48.982
"We"? You said you
were in love with me.

00:14:49.086 --> 00:14:51.145
You didn't say l
felt the same way.

00:14:51.188 --> 00:14:52.678
If you hadn't returned
the feelings,

00:14:52.723 --> 00:14:54.281
do you really think
l would have taken

00:14:54.324 --> 00:14:56.053
such a terrible risk
to get back to you?

00:14:59.496 --> 00:15:02.294
Let's take it
one step at a time.

00:15:02.332 --> 00:15:04.163
How did you get on our ship?

00:15:04.201 --> 00:15:05.259
That was easy.

00:15:05.302 --> 00:15:07.293
The hard part was looking
for the runaway

00:15:07.337 --> 00:15:08.668
without anyone finding me.

00:15:08.706 --> 00:15:10.799
L managed two days on the ship
before l triggered

00:15:10.841 --> 00:15:12.934
an intruder alert
and lost my cloak.

00:15:13.043 --> 00:15:14.704
And then what happened?

00:15:14.745 --> 00:15:17.373
And then l met you.

00:15:38.769 --> 00:15:40.100
Wrong direction.

00:15:42.106 --> 00:15:43.835
L don't want to hurt you.

00:15:43.874 --> 00:15:45.341
Put your weapon down.

00:15:45.375 --> 00:15:47.707
On my ship,
l give the orders.

00:15:47.745 --> 00:15:48.939
Put yours down.

00:15:48.979 --> 00:15:51.277
L don't mean you any harm.

00:15:51.315 --> 00:15:53.374
You have a stowaway
on board.

00:15:53.417 --> 00:15:55.681
L'll retrieve him, and
we'll be on our way.

00:15:55.719 --> 00:15:57.346
That's not the way
we do things here.

00:15:57.387 --> 00:16:00.288
Chakotay to Tuvok.
L'm in Cargo Bay 2.

00:16:00.324 --> 00:16:02.292
L have our intruder.

00:16:02.326 --> 00:16:04.260
Understood, Commander.

00:16:04.294 --> 00:16:06.922
You're about to find yourself
outnumbered.

00:16:07.030 --> 00:16:08.827
If you want
to give me your weapon

00:16:08.866 --> 00:16:12.597
and explain what's going on,
l'll listen.

00:16:22.913 --> 00:16:25.108
L felt an attraction right away,

00:16:25.149 --> 00:16:27.947
but l couldn't afford
to get distracted.

00:16:27.985 --> 00:16:29.213
L had work to do.

00:16:29.253 --> 00:16:32.051
And l didn't know
if you felt it, too.

00:16:32.089 --> 00:16:33.954
What happened next?

00:16:34.024 --> 00:16:37.926
You took me
to Captain Janeway.

00:16:37.961 --> 00:16:39.792
L explained the situation.

00:16:39.830 --> 00:16:41.957
She didn't like the idea
of a stowaway

00:16:41.999 --> 00:16:44.126
on her ship,
so she told you and Tuvok

00:16:44.168 --> 00:16:45.965
to work with me
to flush him out.

00:16:46.003 --> 00:16:47.095
And did we?

00:16:47.137 --> 00:16:50.334
You keep trying
to jump to the end.

00:16:50.374 --> 00:16:52.342
You're skipping all the parts
about us.

00:16:52.376 --> 00:16:54.469
And you keep trying to
talk about your feelings.

00:16:54.511 --> 00:16:56.240
L'd rather you
stick to the events,

00:16:56.280 --> 00:16:57.941
not the emotions
surrounding them.

00:16:57.981 --> 00:16:59.972
Why?

00:17:00.050 --> 00:17:02.177
Does it make you uncomfortable?

00:17:03.720 --> 00:17:05.688
L don't want to play this game.

00:17:05.722 --> 00:17:07.383
L've been assigned
to talk to you...

00:17:07.424 --> 00:17:10.120
to figure out whether or not
you're telling the truth.

00:17:10.160 --> 00:17:13.561
Even if you are,
l have no memory of meeting you

00:17:13.597 --> 00:17:15.622
and l certainly have no memory
of feeling anything

00:17:15.666 --> 00:17:16.928
for you.

00:17:16.967 --> 00:17:18.127
You might remember
a relationship

00:17:18.168 --> 00:17:20.659
between us,
but as far as l'm concerned...

00:17:20.704 --> 00:17:23.935
it didn't exist.

00:17:24.041 --> 00:17:26.100
L see.

00:17:35.152 --> 00:17:36.380
L'm sorry.

00:17:36.420 --> 00:17:38.888
L just want to make
it clear how l feel.

00:17:40.657 --> 00:17:42.716
Of course.

00:17:42.759 --> 00:17:45.227
Is there anything
l can do for you?

00:17:48.065 --> 00:17:50.226
Can l have your pudding?

00:17:54.004 --> 00:17:55.699
Gladly.

00:17:55.739 --> 00:17:57.229
Then you're forgiven.

00:17:59.743 --> 00:18:00.710
Chakotay and Kellin,

00:18:00.744 --> 00:18:02.006
report to the Bridge
immediately.

00:18:02.045 --> 00:18:04.206
It's the tracers.
They've found me.

00:18:13.824 --> 00:18:15.689
We don't detect any ships.

00:18:15.726 --> 00:18:18.092
L'm assuming these are
your people in cloaked vessels.

00:18:18.128 --> 00:18:19.789
They've come
to take me back.

00:18:19.830 --> 00:18:21.092
Harry, hail them.

00:18:21.131 --> 00:18:22.029
They won't answer.

00:18:22.065 --> 00:18:23.293
She's right, Captain.

00:18:23.333 --> 00:18:24.925
No response.

00:18:26.136 --> 00:18:27.433
Their weapons
are going

00:18:27.471 --> 00:18:29.063
through our shields
as if they weren't there.

00:18:29.106 --> 00:18:31.802
Match shields to the frequency
of their particle beams.

00:18:33.510 --> 00:18:34.943
No effect.

00:18:35.012 --> 00:18:37.378
Shield strength
down to 29 percent.

00:18:37.414 --> 00:18:39.473
They'll keep firing
until you surrender

00:18:39.516 --> 00:18:42.041
or until l contact them
and agree to come back.

00:18:42.085 --> 00:18:43.609
Do you still want
to stay with us?

00:18:43.654 --> 00:18:45.383
Yes.

00:18:45.422 --> 00:18:46.821
All right. Tom,

00:18:46.857 --> 00:18:47.949
get us out of here.

00:18:47.991 --> 00:18:50.516
That last volley
damaged our propulsion systems.

00:18:50.560 --> 00:18:51.788
We have thrusters only.

00:18:51.828 --> 00:18:53.955
Captain, if you'll
let me have access

00:18:54.031 --> 00:18:55.430
to your sensor systems,

00:18:55.465 --> 00:18:57.490
l can modify them
to detect the ships.

00:18:57.534 --> 00:18:59.297
Do it.

00:18:59.336 --> 00:19:01.896
This is the moment,
Chakotay.

00:19:01.972 --> 00:19:03.906
Either we give her up
or we fire back.

00:19:03.941 --> 00:19:04.999
Which one is it?

00:19:07.544 --> 00:19:10.206
Fire.

00:19:10.247 --> 00:19:11.179
L think you might

00:19:11.214 --> 00:19:12.181
be able to detect
them now,

00:19:12.215 --> 00:19:13.182
but only for
a minute or two.

00:19:13.216 --> 00:19:14.183
Harry.

00:19:14.217 --> 00:19:15.809
Affirmative.
Two heavily armed ships

00:19:15.852 --> 00:19:17.251
off the port bow.

00:19:17.287 --> 00:19:18.447
Can we get them on screen?

00:19:20.257 --> 00:19:21.349
That's the best l can do.

00:19:24.995 --> 00:19:26.462
Tuvok.

00:19:26.496 --> 00:19:28.020
Target their weapon systems.

00:19:29.199 --> 00:19:30.461
Firing.

00:19:36.840 --> 00:19:38.501
Well done.

00:19:38.542 --> 00:19:40.339
Stand down Red Alert.

00:19:40.377 --> 00:19:43.244
Well, it seems we've
granted you asylum.

00:19:43.280 --> 00:19:44.679
Now you'll have to give

00:19:44.715 --> 00:19:46.945
some thought to what
you want to do.

00:19:48.151 --> 00:19:49.948
L'd prefer to remain on board.

00:19:50.053 --> 00:19:51.179
Consider that
carefully.

00:19:51.221 --> 00:19:53.052
We're heading
for the Alpha Quadrant.

00:19:53.090 --> 00:19:55.285
Before long, we will be
so far from your world

00:19:55.325 --> 00:19:56.314
that if you change your mind,

00:19:56.360 --> 00:19:57.520
you wouldn't be able
to get back.

00:19:57.561 --> 00:20:00.962
L won't change my mind,
but l must warn you...

00:20:00.998 --> 00:20:03.193
the tracers won't give up
that easily.

00:20:03.233 --> 00:20:04.825
Your ship is still at risk.

00:20:04.868 --> 00:20:06.802
Nothing we haven't
faced before.

00:20:06.837 --> 00:20:08.964
L was only able to make
a temporary modification

00:20:09.039 --> 00:20:10.472
to your sensors.

00:20:10.507 --> 00:20:12.975
If you'd let me access
your astrometric processors,

00:20:13.010 --> 00:20:14.978
l could make
that modification permanent.

00:20:15.045 --> 00:20:16.979
You'll need a command
officer with you

00:20:17.014 --> 00:20:18.743
to override the
security lockouts.

00:20:18.782 --> 00:20:20.044
L can do that, Captain.

00:20:21.051 --> 00:20:22.040
Go ahead.

00:20:24.988 --> 00:20:26.455
Tom, coordinate
with Engineering

00:20:26.490 --> 00:20:28.822
to get the propulsion systems
back on line.

00:20:28.859 --> 00:20:30.156
L'm on it, Captain.

00:20:40.570 --> 00:20:42.504
We'll have to climb
up to Deck 10.

00:20:45.108 --> 00:20:46.200
Is something wrong?

00:20:50.147 --> 00:20:52.547
L can't relax
until we're far enough away

00:20:52.582 --> 00:20:55.142
that they realize
they can't get me back...

00:20:55.185 --> 00:20:58.780
and to my knowledge,
that's never happened before.

00:20:58.822 --> 00:21:01.484
There's always
a first time.

00:21:01.525 --> 00:21:03.959
L have a high
security clearance.

00:21:03.994 --> 00:21:05.655
They'll be afraid
l'm going to do

00:21:05.695 --> 00:21:07.253
exactly what l'm about to do...

00:21:07.297 --> 00:21:09.527
show you how to detect them.

00:21:12.035 --> 00:21:13.525
Look at it this way.

00:21:13.570 --> 00:21:15.197
If they do figure out
we can spot them,

00:21:15.238 --> 00:21:16.364
they might realize

00:21:16.406 --> 00:21:18.533
they aren't going to be
able to take you back.

00:21:22.846 --> 00:21:25.144
You're such a kind person.

00:21:25.182 --> 00:21:27.207
That's what l
remembered most.

00:21:30.220 --> 00:21:33.280
It's what made me
turn around and come back.

00:21:33.323 --> 00:21:36.884
And sometime...

00:21:36.927 --> 00:21:39.896
you might be interested in...

00:21:39.930 --> 00:21:43.195
hearing about
our last night together.

00:21:51.641 --> 00:21:53.404
Evening, Commander.

00:21:53.443 --> 00:21:56.207
Craving
a late-night snack?

00:21:56.246 --> 00:21:58.714
No. Something
to help me sleep.

00:21:58.748 --> 00:22:00.739
Got any ideas?

00:22:00.784 --> 00:22:04.777
L know humans think
warm milk will do it.

00:22:04.821 --> 00:22:07.289
Frankly,
l find it repulsive.

00:22:07.324 --> 00:22:08.757
L agree.

00:22:08.792 --> 00:22:10.487
What's available
in the tea area?

00:22:10.527 --> 00:22:12.859
Herbal is best.

00:22:12.896 --> 00:22:16.457
L have several
Terran varieties, uh...

00:22:16.500 --> 00:22:19.469
as well as some
more exotic blends.

00:22:19.503 --> 00:22:21.061
Just mix me up
whatever you think

00:22:21.104 --> 00:22:22.162
is the most relaxing.

00:22:25.542 --> 00:22:26.941
Problems?

00:22:28.378 --> 00:22:30.710
Forgive me.
L wasn't trying to pry.

00:22:32.082 --> 00:22:33.071
L know that.

00:22:33.116 --> 00:22:34.811
L'm just not sure
how to answer you.

00:22:34.851 --> 00:22:38.184
How's our guest adapting
to life on Voyager?

00:22:38.221 --> 00:22:39.916
Quite well, l think.

00:22:39.956 --> 00:22:41.548
She must be happy
to be here.

00:22:41.591 --> 00:22:43.183
L'm sure she is.

00:22:47.397 --> 00:22:49.365
Forgive me, Commander...

00:22:51.001 --> 00:22:54.459
but sometimes it's best
to be straightforward.

00:22:54.504 --> 00:22:57.371
It's obvious
how she feels about you...

00:22:57.407 --> 00:22:58.704
to me, at least.

00:22:58.742 --> 00:23:00.505
L see how she looks at you.

00:23:00.544 --> 00:23:03.638
Might that be the source
of your consternation?

00:23:06.950 --> 00:23:08.713
She says she, or rather

00:23:08.752 --> 00:23:11.687
we fell in love when
she was here before.

00:23:11.721 --> 00:23:13.586
Since l can't
remember any of that,

00:23:13.623 --> 00:23:15.056
l don't know if it's true,

00:23:15.091 --> 00:23:17.218
but somehow, it's
hard to believe.

00:23:17.260 --> 00:23:19.091
Why is that?

00:23:19.129 --> 00:23:20.096
L don't know.

00:23:20.130 --> 00:23:22.098
It just doesn't seem like me.

00:23:22.132 --> 00:23:24.100
L'm still suspicious of her.

00:23:24.134 --> 00:23:26.466
L don't know
if she's using me in some way

00:23:26.503 --> 00:23:28.767
just for her own purposes.

00:23:28.805 --> 00:23:31.239
You don't trust her.

00:23:32.842 --> 00:23:34.241
Not really.

00:23:39.549 --> 00:23:42.712
May l suggest...

00:23:42.752 --> 00:23:45.585
that maybe it's yourself
you don't trust?

00:23:45.622 --> 00:23:47.749
Your own feelings
that you're afraid of?

00:23:49.759 --> 00:23:51.818
Sweet dreams.

00:24:12.649 --> 00:24:14.810
L couldn't sleep.

00:24:14.851 --> 00:24:17.081
L need to talk to you.

00:24:17.120 --> 00:24:19.145
May l come in?

00:24:24.027 --> 00:24:25.289
L was just wondering

00:24:25.328 --> 00:24:27.319
if you still had
doubts about me

00:24:27.364 --> 00:24:31.061
or if you believe what
l told you about us.

00:24:32.802 --> 00:24:35.168
Your story seems
to have been verified.

00:24:35.205 --> 00:24:37.435
L believe you're
telling the truth.

00:24:37.474 --> 00:24:39.032
And the rest of it?

00:24:40.744 --> 00:24:42.302
What about us?

00:24:50.186 --> 00:24:52.746
L'm not one to hold back,
as you may have noticed,

00:24:52.789 --> 00:24:54.814
so l'll get to the point.

00:24:54.858 --> 00:24:57.884
L came here because of you.

00:24:57.927 --> 00:25:01.419
L knew you wouldn't
remember me,

00:25:01.464 --> 00:25:03.796
but l was sure
we could regain

00:25:03.833 --> 00:25:06.461
the feelings
we had before.

00:25:06.503 --> 00:25:09.370
They were there...

00:25:09.406 --> 00:25:12.569
and they were real...

00:25:12.609 --> 00:25:16.177
but now l'm not so sure.

00:25:17.578 --> 00:25:19.102
My being here puts

00:25:19.146 --> 00:25:21.239
this ship at risk.

00:25:21.282 --> 00:25:24.513
It's better for everyone
if l go back to Ramura.

00:25:26.921 --> 00:25:29.788
So please be honest.

00:25:29.823 --> 00:25:33.691
If you feel nothing for me...

00:25:33.727 --> 00:25:36.389
just tell me...

00:25:36.430 --> 00:25:38.057
and l'll leave.

00:25:43.204 --> 00:25:45.502
Don't go.

00:25:57.451 --> 00:25:59.976
It's called "ice cream"?

00:26:00.087 --> 00:26:01.418
L'm surprised
you didn't have any

00:26:01.455 --> 00:26:02.922
the last time you were here.

00:26:02.990 --> 00:26:05.515
L could eat
this every day.

00:26:05.559 --> 00:26:07.959
Then you should.

00:26:11.899 --> 00:26:14.026
Voyager's a very...

00:26:14.068 --> 00:26:15.797
powerful ship.

00:26:15.836 --> 00:26:18.498
And very fast.

00:26:18.539 --> 00:26:21.064
We've met people
with ships that are faster

00:26:21.108 --> 00:26:22.666
and more powerful,

00:26:22.710 --> 00:26:24.678
but Voyager's always
managed to be a match

00:26:24.712 --> 00:26:25.736
for the best of them.

00:26:30.017 --> 00:26:32.212
Ramuran vessels are fast.

00:26:34.555 --> 00:26:37.046
They could stay up
with this ship.

00:26:37.091 --> 00:26:39.218
Kellin...

00:26:39.260 --> 00:26:41.251
we'll keep you safe.

00:26:41.295 --> 00:26:42.694
That's a promise.

00:26:42.730 --> 00:26:45.722
A tracer never goes
home empty-handed.

00:26:45.766 --> 00:26:48.234
The disgrace would be too great.

00:26:48.269 --> 00:26:49.497
When l was here before,

00:26:49.536 --> 00:26:51.970
l'd been tracking that man
for almost a year.

00:26:52.039 --> 00:26:53.700
But you know all the tricks.

00:26:53.741 --> 00:26:54.969
You can use them
against anyone

00:26:55.009 --> 00:26:56.237
who tries to come after you.

00:27:03.083 --> 00:27:04.345
You said you were
going to tell me

00:27:04.385 --> 00:27:05.613
about our last night together.

00:27:06.620 --> 00:27:08.417
Let me show you.

00:27:10.190 --> 00:27:13.648
You were sitting here
in this chair...

00:27:15.296 --> 00:27:18.197
and I...

00:27:18.232 --> 00:27:20.462
was here.

00:27:20.501 --> 00:27:23.698
And we were drinking
something with bubbles.

00:27:23.737 --> 00:27:25.534
Champagne?

00:27:25.572 --> 00:27:26.903
Yes.

00:27:26.940 --> 00:27:28.669
L wanted to celebrate.

00:27:28.709 --> 00:27:31.507
L'd caught my runaway that day
with your help.

00:27:31.545 --> 00:27:32.569
How was that?

00:27:32.613 --> 00:27:34.046
You came up with the idea

00:27:34.081 --> 00:27:35.946
of using a magneton sweep

00:27:35.983 --> 00:27:37.848
to disrupt his
polarization cloak.

00:27:37.885 --> 00:27:39.614
We knew he'd be
watching me closely,

00:27:39.653 --> 00:27:42.884
so... we tricked him.

00:27:47.061 --> 00:27:49.529
L'm sorry you didn't
get your fugitive.

00:27:49.563 --> 00:27:51.895
He must have jumped
to another ship

00:27:51.932 --> 00:27:54.560
while Voyager was in
orbit of Mikah last week.

00:27:54.601 --> 00:27:56.262
L'll find him eventually.

00:27:56.303 --> 00:27:58.635
If you think we could be
of any more help, let me know.

00:27:58.672 --> 00:27:59.969
Thank you, Commander.

00:28:00.074 --> 00:28:01.336
This is my problem.

00:28:01.375 --> 00:28:03.366
L'll handle it from now on.

00:28:04.411 --> 00:28:06.811
Just beam me
back to my ship

00:28:06.847 --> 00:28:09.145
and l'll backtrack to Mikah.

00:28:09.183 --> 00:28:12.778
Good-bye, and thank you again.

00:28:12.820 --> 00:28:14.253
Ready to energize.

00:28:24.465 --> 00:28:25.557
Hello, Resket.

00:28:25.599 --> 00:28:27.123
You were
a real challenge.

00:28:27.167 --> 00:28:28.259
L haven't had
the chance

00:28:28.302 --> 00:28:29.735
to welcome you to Voyager.

00:28:29.770 --> 00:28:31.635
Too bad you'll
be leaving so soon.

00:28:33.540 --> 00:28:35.030
We put him in the brig.

00:28:35.075 --> 00:28:37.066
Once l used
the neurolytic emitter on him,

00:28:37.111 --> 00:28:39.409
he was only too happy
to be going home again.

00:28:39.446 --> 00:28:41.141
Neurolytic emitter.

00:28:41.181 --> 00:28:42.580
We use it on runaways.

00:28:42.616 --> 00:28:45.050
It wipes their memories
of the outside world.

00:28:45.085 --> 00:28:48.316
So we were
celebrating?

00:28:48.355 --> 00:28:51.153
You'd become much more
than a friend to me,

00:28:51.191 --> 00:28:52.590
but l knew
l had to go home,

00:28:52.626 --> 00:28:54.651
and you'd forget about me
within hours.

00:28:54.695 --> 00:28:57.289
So l took the initiative.

00:28:57.331 --> 00:28:59.128
More than usual?

00:28:59.166 --> 00:29:01.031
Oh, yes.

00:29:03.570 --> 00:29:05.561
L moved closer to you...

00:29:07.474 --> 00:29:11.808
l thanked you profusely
for all your help,

00:29:11.845 --> 00:29:14.143
told you that l couldn't
have done it without you...

00:29:20.254 --> 00:29:22.745
and l touched you.

00:29:22.790 --> 00:29:26.692
L told you I...
l cared very much for you...

00:29:28.362 --> 00:29:30.990
and that l wanted something
to remember you by.

00:29:33.734 --> 00:29:35.326
And then l did this.

00:29:58.926 --> 00:30:01.360
That's when l knew
you felt the same way.

00:30:03.797 --> 00:30:06.322
But it didn't matter
because l still had to go.

00:30:08.635 --> 00:30:10.432
But now you don't.

00:30:26.620 --> 00:30:28.645
If Kellin's going
to be with us,

00:30:28.689 --> 00:30:30.350
the Captain wants her
to serve a function...

00:30:30.390 --> 00:30:31.789
to contribute in some way.

00:30:31.825 --> 00:30:33.486
A reasonable
expectation.

00:30:33.527 --> 00:30:34.824
What are her skills?

00:30:34.862 --> 00:30:38.093
Basically, she was a security
operative for her people.

00:30:38.131 --> 00:30:39.996
She's a trained expert
in weaponry,

00:30:40.100 --> 00:30:42.534
surveillance,
fighting skills.

00:30:42.569 --> 00:30:44.662
Any idea where she
might fit in?

00:30:44.705 --> 00:30:47.606
Mr. Neelix could use an
assistant in the Mess Hall.

00:30:47.641 --> 00:30:51.702
Tuvok, that was a joke.

00:30:51.745 --> 00:30:53.940
Don't deny it...
you were trying to be funny.

00:30:53.981 --> 00:30:56.609
If you choose to interpret
my remark as humorous,

00:30:56.650 --> 00:30:57.878
that is your decision.

00:30:57.918 --> 00:30:59.852
L do and it was.

00:30:59.887 --> 00:31:01.616
It's perfectly logical.

00:31:01.655 --> 00:31:02.781
All the qualities
you mentioned

00:31:02.823 --> 00:31:03.915
would help in
defending Neelix

00:31:03.957 --> 00:31:05.788
against the periodic
wrath of the crew.

00:31:06.994 --> 00:31:09.292
Maybe so, but don't you
think she'd be better off

00:31:09.329 --> 00:31:11.194
as a member
of your security detail?

00:31:11.231 --> 00:31:13.199
Perhaps. L'll assign
her to a team

00:31:13.233 --> 00:31:15.098
and let her
observe for a week.

00:31:15.135 --> 00:31:17.501
At the end of that time,
l'll evaluate her situation.

00:31:17.538 --> 00:31:18.698
Good enough.

00:31:18.739 --> 00:31:21.731
Commander, l've been giving
some thought to the fact

00:31:21.775 --> 00:31:24.141
that the Ramuran ships
might be in pursuit

00:31:24.177 --> 00:31:25.542
and could attack us again.

00:31:25.579 --> 00:31:27.410
L've given that
some thought myself.

00:31:27.447 --> 00:31:28.971
Their proton weapons

00:31:29.016 --> 00:31:30.813
were particularly
effective against us.

00:31:30.851 --> 00:31:33.843
If Kellin would work
with Seven and Ensign Kim,

00:31:33.887 --> 00:31:34.979
perhaps we could devise

00:31:35.022 --> 00:31:36.455
a strategy to
defend ourselves.

00:31:36.490 --> 00:31:37.980
L'm sure she'd be happy
to do that.

00:31:38.025 --> 00:31:39.856
Have her report
to Astrometrics

00:31:39.893 --> 00:31:41.121
at 1300 hours.

00:31:49.369 --> 00:31:52.338
L've downloaded data
from our tactical logs.

00:31:52.372 --> 00:31:54.272
You can access it
from this console.

00:31:57.945 --> 00:32:00.436
Our weapons are proton-
based particle beams,

00:32:00.480 --> 00:32:01.777
very tightly focused.

00:32:01.815 --> 00:32:04.875
It's like being hit
with thousands of needles.

00:32:04.918 --> 00:32:06.215
They can penetrate
any shield

00:32:06.253 --> 00:32:08.153
even if the modulations
are changed.

00:32:08.188 --> 00:32:09.951
Very clever.

00:32:10.057 --> 00:32:12.525
No defense has ever
stopped these weapons.

00:32:12.559 --> 00:32:14.527
Then maybe we're
about to make history.

00:32:14.561 --> 00:32:15.892
You've found a way
to counteract them?

00:32:15.929 --> 00:32:17.396
L think so.

00:32:17.431 --> 00:32:19.058
The trick is to scatter
those beams a little,

00:32:19.099 --> 00:32:21.226
make it harder for them
to penetrate the shields.

00:32:21.268 --> 00:32:23.964
L think we could do that
by tying the baryon sensors

00:32:24.004 --> 00:32:25.596
into Deflector Control.

00:32:25.639 --> 00:32:27.197
Here's what l have in mind.

00:32:27.240 --> 00:32:28.969
Why don't you look this over
and let me know what you think?

00:32:29.042 --> 00:32:30.270
L'll do it right away.

00:32:30.310 --> 00:32:33.370
By the way, l hear Chakotay
recommended you to Tuvok

00:32:33.413 --> 00:32:35.142
to serve on a security detail.

00:32:35.182 --> 00:32:37.480
L want to help out
in some way.

00:32:37.517 --> 00:32:38.484
A word of advice.

00:32:38.518 --> 00:32:40.349
Volunteer for Beta Squad;
they're the best team.

00:32:40.387 --> 00:32:41.513
You'll learn a lot from them.

00:32:41.555 --> 00:32:43.318
L will. Thank you.

00:32:47.294 --> 00:32:49.319
When you mentioned
Commander Chakotay's name,

00:32:49.363 --> 00:32:50.796
she flushed.

00:32:50.831 --> 00:32:52.628
He did the same
when he saw her.

00:32:52.666 --> 00:32:54.258
What are you saying?

00:32:54.301 --> 00:32:57.236
L suspect the Commander
and Kellin are engaged

00:32:57.270 --> 00:32:58.999
in a courtship ritual.

00:32:59.072 --> 00:33:01.563
It seems an unnecessary
and complicated precursor

00:33:01.608 --> 00:33:03.200
to the act of procreation.

00:33:04.578 --> 00:33:06.375
L know you think so,

00:33:06.413 --> 00:33:09.109
but trust me, some people
need those rituals.

00:33:10.550 --> 00:33:11.710
Explain.

00:33:11.752 --> 00:33:14.243
It's... it's usually considered
a good idea

00:33:14.287 --> 00:33:16.949
if two people get to know
each other a little

00:33:16.990 --> 00:33:20.187
before they become... intimate.

00:33:20.227 --> 00:33:21.717
Why is that?

00:33:23.096 --> 00:33:25.121
Because it's more comfortable.

00:33:25.165 --> 00:33:28.328
Uh, you spend some time
together, you laugh, you talk.

00:33:28.368 --> 00:33:30.768
That makes it easier to...

00:33:30.804 --> 00:33:32.601
to get closer.

00:33:32.639 --> 00:33:34.937
But the end result is the same,
is it not?

00:33:36.276 --> 00:33:37.470
Well, l guess so.

00:33:37.511 --> 00:33:40.446
Then l fail to see what is
accomplished by all the talk.

00:33:40.480 --> 00:33:43.313
Seven, if you don't get it,
then l can't explain it to you.

00:33:43.350 --> 00:33:45.284
Obviously.

00:34:32.165 --> 00:34:33.462
L should have known.

00:34:33.500 --> 00:34:34.797
They must have gotten
somebody on board

00:34:34.835 --> 00:34:35.802
during the battle.

00:34:35.836 --> 00:34:36.928
You're jumping
to conclusions.

00:34:36.970 --> 00:34:38.335
No. There's a tracer.

00:34:38.371 --> 00:34:40.134
He's here, he's
come for me.

00:34:40.173 --> 00:34:41.834
That broken vase
was a warning.

00:34:41.875 --> 00:34:43.206
We'll protect you.

00:34:43.243 --> 00:34:44.904
L'm not going to let
anything happen to you.

00:34:44.945 --> 00:34:46.537
- It's too late.
- No!

00:34:46.580 --> 00:34:48.241
We can use
the same magneton sweep

00:34:48.281 --> 00:34:49.748
we used to flush out Resket.

00:34:49.783 --> 00:34:51.842
We'll find this one
and send him on his way.

00:34:53.086 --> 00:34:55.281
L'm afraid
l can't let that happen.

00:34:55.322 --> 00:34:56.289
Curneth, don't.

00:34:56.323 --> 00:34:57.654
Chakotay to Security.

00:34:57.691 --> 00:34:59.488
Intruder alert,
my quarters.

00:34:59.526 --> 00:35:03.189
Please, l beg you,
don't do this.

00:35:03.230 --> 00:35:05.698
You know better
than to ask that, Kellin.

00:35:05.732 --> 00:35:07.393
No!

00:35:07.434 --> 00:35:08.492
Drop it!

00:35:08.535 --> 00:35:09.524
Drop it!

00:35:09.569 --> 00:35:11.935
You're too late.

00:35:11.972 --> 00:35:13.599
She's already
beginning to forget

00:35:13.640 --> 00:35:15.335
everything that's happened here.

00:35:47.140 --> 00:35:49.734
The Doctor says
there's nothing he can do.

00:35:49.776 --> 00:35:51.869
Your recent memories
have already begun to fade.

00:35:51.912 --> 00:35:54.312
Don't let this
happen, please.

00:35:54.347 --> 00:35:55.871
Don't let this happen.

00:35:55.916 --> 00:35:59.545
Do you have any idea
how we can reverse the effect?

00:36:02.989 --> 00:36:05.014
Promise me...

00:36:05.058 --> 00:36:07.618
if l forget
why l'm here,

00:36:07.661 --> 00:36:11.119
if l forget you...

00:36:11.164 --> 00:36:14.565
do what l did...

00:36:14.601 --> 00:36:17.468
and you'll tell me
all about us...

00:36:17.504 --> 00:36:21.702
and you'll help
me to remember.

00:36:21.741 --> 00:36:26.644
L will, but l'm going
to try to do more than that.

00:36:42.228 --> 00:36:44.162
Can the effects
of the neurolytic emitter

00:36:44.197 --> 00:36:45.596
be reversed?

00:36:45.631 --> 00:36:47.292
Reversed?

00:36:47.333 --> 00:36:49.198
L have no idea.

00:36:49.235 --> 00:36:51.669
As far as l know,
no one's ever tried.

00:36:51.704 --> 00:36:53.433
Then l'll be the first.

00:36:53.472 --> 00:36:55.235
Tell me how the emitter works...

00:36:55.274 --> 00:36:56.707
how it affects
the memory centers.

00:36:56.742 --> 00:36:59.836
You sound desperate, Commander.

00:36:59.879 --> 00:37:02.279
Does Kellin mean
that much to you?

00:37:02.315 --> 00:37:03.748
What you're doing is wrong.

00:37:03.783 --> 00:37:05.011
She wants to stay here.

00:37:05.051 --> 00:37:07.315
This is futile.

00:37:07.353 --> 00:37:10.220
Even if l knew
how the emitter works,

00:37:10.256 --> 00:37:12.224
l wouldn't tell you.

00:37:24.003 --> 00:37:26.198
You have no right
to do this.

00:37:26.239 --> 00:37:27.797
L have every right.

00:37:27.840 --> 00:37:31.799
The laws on our world are
very specific about that.

00:37:31.844 --> 00:37:33.937
No one may leave.

00:37:33.980 --> 00:37:35.914
No one may reveal
anything about us

00:37:35.948 --> 00:37:37.142
to the outside world.

00:37:37.183 --> 00:37:40.084
Kellin has violated
both of those edicts.

00:37:40.119 --> 00:37:41.950
Returning her will
serve as a deterrent

00:37:41.988 --> 00:37:44.479
to others who might
think of leaving.

00:37:46.292 --> 00:37:47.418
Did it ever occur to you

00:37:47.460 --> 00:37:49.394
that the fact that so many
people want to leave might mean

00:37:49.428 --> 00:37:51.225
that there's something wrong
with your society?

00:37:51.264 --> 00:37:54.597
We have a strong
and cohesive society

00:37:54.634 --> 00:37:57.694
because of our efforts
to keep it that way.

00:37:57.737 --> 00:37:59.967
A few runaways among millions

00:38:00.039 --> 00:38:01.802
hardly indicates
a problem.

00:38:01.841 --> 00:38:03.138
If there are so few...

00:38:05.745 --> 00:38:07.178
why not let them go?

00:38:07.213 --> 00:38:10.478
That would suggest that
we don't care about them.

00:38:10.516 --> 00:38:13.212
What a terrible message.

00:38:13.252 --> 00:38:17.211
You may have wiped her memory,
but Kellin's not going back.

00:38:17.256 --> 00:38:20.089
Maybe we should wait and
see if that's what happens.

00:38:20.126 --> 00:38:21.286
She made it

00:38:21.327 --> 00:38:23.352
clear to me
that she wants to stay here.

00:38:23.396 --> 00:38:25.921
So maybe you
should start practicing

00:38:25.998 --> 00:38:27.625
what you're going
to tell your superiors.

00:38:45.251 --> 00:38:47.378
Yes?

00:38:52.425 --> 00:38:54.222
The Doctor told me
he'd released you.

00:38:54.260 --> 00:38:55.284
How are you feeling?

00:38:55.328 --> 00:38:57.159
L'm fine.

00:38:57.196 --> 00:38:59.323
Do l know you?

00:39:01.400 --> 00:39:03.493
Yes.

00:39:03.536 --> 00:39:04.764
At least, you did.

00:39:08.507 --> 00:39:09.906
You'll have to forgive me,

00:39:09.975 --> 00:39:11.670
but l don't remember
how l got here

00:39:11.711 --> 00:39:13.611
or anything else
that's happened

00:39:13.646 --> 00:39:15.511
in at least the
past few weeks.

00:39:15.548 --> 00:39:17.482
L know.

00:39:17.516 --> 00:39:21.612
L hope l wasn't throwing
things in a fit of rage.

00:39:21.654 --> 00:39:23.417
No.

00:39:23.456 --> 00:39:27.256
L assume a tracer is
here to take me back.

00:39:27.293 --> 00:39:28.988
That's right.

00:39:30.529 --> 00:39:31.996
But...

00:39:36.102 --> 00:39:37.831
what l'm going to say
will sound strange...

00:39:42.408 --> 00:39:45.070
but it's what you
asked me to do

00:39:45.111 --> 00:39:47.477
before you lost
your memories.

00:39:47.546 --> 00:39:49.070
You came here
about a month ago

00:39:49.115 --> 00:39:51.106
looking for a runaway.

00:39:51.150 --> 00:39:54.677
After you left with him,
you decided to come back.

00:39:54.720 --> 00:39:57.655
But if l finished
my assignment,

00:39:57.690 --> 00:39:58.850
why would l come back here?

00:39:58.891 --> 00:40:00.119
Because...

00:40:01.827 --> 00:40:04.057
you'd fallen
in love with me.

00:40:08.067 --> 00:40:09.534
Forgive me.

00:40:09.568 --> 00:40:11.399
You're... certainly attractive,

00:40:11.437 --> 00:40:13.405
but... what
you're telling me

00:40:13.439 --> 00:40:15.566
seems very unlikely.

00:40:15.608 --> 00:40:17.473
But it's what
happened.

00:40:17.510 --> 00:40:20.968
We started to
work together...

00:40:21.080 --> 00:40:24.641
and l began to realize
how unique you are.

00:40:24.683 --> 00:40:27.982
Before long, l couldn't
get you out of my mind.

00:40:28.053 --> 00:40:32.217
Are you saying that you fell
in love with me as well?

00:40:32.258 --> 00:40:35.125
Yes.

00:40:35.161 --> 00:40:38.653
And then we realized
the tracer was on board.

00:40:38.697 --> 00:40:40.688
After he used
the emitter on you,

00:40:40.733 --> 00:40:43.167
you made me promise to
tell you all of this,

00:40:43.202 --> 00:40:45.136
so you would know what
happened between us.

00:40:47.173 --> 00:40:48.470
This is...

00:40:48.507 --> 00:40:50.304
a little unsettling.

00:40:52.645 --> 00:40:54.340
What is it
you want from me?

00:40:56.182 --> 00:40:58.548
Kellin...

00:40:58.584 --> 00:41:00.882
don't go back
with the tracer.

00:41:00.920 --> 00:41:03.548
Stay here for a while,
at least for a few days.

00:41:03.589 --> 00:41:07.958
We can get to know
each other again.

00:41:08.027 --> 00:41:12.430
L honestly can't imagine
what would be served by that.

00:41:12.465 --> 00:41:14.194
L have to go home.

00:41:14.233 --> 00:41:15.962
If you stayed...

00:41:16.001 --> 00:41:19.300
you might change
your mind.

00:41:19.338 --> 00:41:21.203
Then that's
all the more reason

00:41:21.240 --> 00:41:23.970
that l should leave now.

00:41:24.009 --> 00:41:27.775
L've violated one
of our most important edicts...

00:41:29.348 --> 00:41:32.215
and l wouldn't want
to make that mistake again.

00:41:37.356 --> 00:41:38.983
L wish...

00:41:44.129 --> 00:41:47.121
l wish we had met
under different circumstances.

00:42:11.357 --> 00:42:13.222
Your ship's ready.

00:42:13.259 --> 00:42:15.056
Thank you,
Commander.

00:42:15.094 --> 00:42:16.857
L've implanted
a computer virus

00:42:16.896 --> 00:42:19.524
to eliminate any reference
to our being here.

00:42:19.565 --> 00:42:21.192
By tomorrow afternoon,

00:42:21.233 --> 00:42:22.427
you'll have forgotten
everything.

00:42:22.468 --> 00:42:24.959
It will be as though
we never existed.

00:42:25.037 --> 00:42:26.504
It's better that way.

00:42:26.539 --> 00:42:28.769
You're such
a kind person.

00:42:28.807 --> 00:42:31.537
L won't forget that.

00:42:33.178 --> 00:42:35.169
L wish you both the best.

00:42:56.435 --> 00:42:58.300
Energize.

00:43:07.212 --> 00:43:12.206
First Officer's Personal Log,
Stardate 51813.4.

00:43:12.251 --> 00:43:15.448
Maybe it would be best,
as the tracer said,

00:43:15.487 --> 00:43:17.648
to forget about Kellin
and the time she spent here,

00:43:17.690 --> 00:43:20.386
but l don't want to do that.

00:43:20.426 --> 00:43:22.485
L want to remember.

00:43:22.528 --> 00:43:24.758
More coffee, Commander?

00:43:24.797 --> 00:43:26.128
No, thanks.

00:43:26.165 --> 00:43:27.962
L'm almost done.

00:43:29.268 --> 00:43:31.532
Strange to
see you using

00:43:31.570 --> 00:43:33.868
those ancient
writing implements.

00:43:33.906 --> 00:43:36.841
Ah, it's the only way
l could get a permanent record

00:43:36.875 --> 00:43:39.139
of what's happened
in the last few days.

00:43:39.178 --> 00:43:41.442
L want to get it down
before l forget it all.

00:43:42.948 --> 00:43:44.279
L'm sorry things

00:43:44.316 --> 00:43:46.011
didn't work
out for you.

00:43:48.454 --> 00:43:51.981
L've been trying
to make sense of it.

00:43:52.024 --> 00:43:53.753
L fell in love with her twice.

00:43:53.792 --> 00:43:55.589
L thought she could do the same.

00:43:55.628 --> 00:43:59.223
We were the same two people
on the same ship.

00:43:59.264 --> 00:44:01.129
Why didn't it happen again?

00:44:01.166 --> 00:44:04.158
L keep going over and over
our last conversation,

00:44:04.203 --> 00:44:05.602
trying to think
if there was

00:44:05.638 --> 00:44:09.506
something l could have said,
could have done...

00:44:09.541 --> 00:44:12.305
but nothing comes to mind.

00:44:12.344 --> 00:44:15.711
Commander, l don't think
you can analyze love.

00:44:15.748 --> 00:44:19.275
It's the greatest mystery
of all.

00:44:19.318 --> 00:44:22.719
No one knows why it
happens or doesn't.

00:44:22.755 --> 00:44:25.553
Love is a chance
combination of elements.

00:44:25.591 --> 00:44:28.958
Any one thing might be enough
to keep it from igniting...

00:44:28.994 --> 00:44:30.825
a mood, a glance...

00:44:30.863 --> 00:44:33.957
a remark.

00:44:34.033 --> 00:44:37.366
And if we could define love...

00:44:37.403 --> 00:44:40.270
predict it...

00:44:40.305 --> 00:44:42.603
it would probably lose
its power.

00:44:44.610 --> 00:44:46.908
L'll let you finish.

00:44:50.115 --> 00:44:51.480
Good night.
